3:["$","p",null,{"children":"Sinusitis occurs when the tissues lining the sinuses become inflamed or swollen. This inflammation can interfere with normal sinus drainage and lead to congestion and pressure."}]
4:["$","p",null,{"children":"Sinusitis may occur after a cold or respiratory infection. Allergies, nasal polyps, a deviated septum and other nasal conditions can also contribute to persistent or recurrent sinus symptoms."}]
